%N A072462 Numbers k such that sigma(k) == 3 (mod 4).
%C A072462 All the terms are squares or twice squares. k = 2^e * m^2, where m is odd, is a term if and only if the number of primes p == 1 (mod 4) with odd valuation v_p(m) is odd for e = 0, and even for e > 0. - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026
